  "title": "Erdős Problem #669",
  "statement": {
    "representation": "markdown-latex",
    "text": "Let $F_k(n)$ be minimal such that for any $n$ points in $\\mathbb{R}^2$ there exist at most $F_k(n)$ many distinct lines passing through at least $k$ of the points, and $f_k(n)$ similarly but with lines passing through exactly $k$ points.\nEstimate $f_k(n)$ and $F_k(n)$ - in particular, determine $\\lim F_k(n)/n^2$ and $\\lim f_k(n)/n^2$.",
